Part - 01

Day 23 Notes – MongoDB + Mongoose

1.Install Mongoose
npm install mongoose

2.Connect to MongoDB
import mongoose from "mongoose";

mongoose.connect(MONGO_URL)
.then(() => console.log("MongoDB Connected"))
.catch((err) => console.log(err));

3.Connection String Format
mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/todoapp?retryWrites=true&w=majority

4.Create Schema + Model
const todoSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
text: String,
completed: { type: Boolean, default: false }
});

const Todo = mongoose.model("Todo", todoSchema);

5.Important Points:
-Schema = structure of data
-Model = used to interact with the database
-Always allow Network Access (0.0.0.0/0) in Atlas for learning
-Database name is written after .net/ (example: /todoapp)

6.Key Point:
Mongoose helps Node.js talk to MongoDB easily.
